## Suppose version 2 has a problem.
Check the release history:
helm history fairy-bake

You should see the installation and upgrade revisions.

## Roll back to the previous revision. If revision 1 is the original installation, run
helm rollback fairy-bake 1

##Check the Deployment:
kubectl get deployments

##Check the image:
kubectl get deployments -o wide

//The Deployment should return to the earlier image configuration, fairy-bake:v1.

Refresh:
http://localhost:8081

we should see the original website version again.

Note that the old image must remain available to the KIND nodes for the rollback to work. In this exercise, we loaded both versions into the cluster.

##Verify the Complete Deployment

Run the following commands:
helm list
helm status fairy-bake
helm history fairy-bake
kubectl get deployments
kubectl get pods
kubectl get services
kubectl get pods -o wide

These commands let you inspect the Helm release and its underlying Kubernetes resources.

##Clean Up the Practical
helm uninstall fairy-bake

## Verify that its application resources are removed:
kubectl get pods

## We can remove the chart directory if you no longer need it:
rm -rf ~/bakery-app/fairy-bake-chart
